+  <!-- ============ 4 Proposed design ============ -->
+  <section id="design">
+    <h2>4 · Proposed design</h2>
+    <ul class="key-points">
+      <li>One immutable route index per map install, shared by every seat. One immutable hazard overlay per episode. A small bounded safe cache per horizon bucket.</li>
+      <li>Every route request is answered synchronously in the same call by a bounded A* over the portal-side graph plus bounded endpoint refinement.</li>
+      <li>The follower reads the legs from the index. The endpoint legs are copied into small fixed per-seat buffers. A deterministic eight-octant rule steers when no advancing route exists.</li>
+      <li>All route choice is integer arithmetic with no clocks, threads, pointer identity or hash-iteration order.</li>
+    </ul>
+
+    <p>In one sentence: build one immutable room/portal route index per map install, attach one immutable zone hazard overlay per episode, answer every route request in the same call with a bounded search over the portal-side graph plus bounded endpoint refinement, execute the selected legs from the index, and steer locally with a deterministic eight-octant rule when no advancing route exists.</p>
