+
+    <h3>Round 1: fact checks and simplifications, all accepted</h3>
+    <p>Fact checks included: the <code>damage</code> versus <code>arrival</code> surface distinction. The derated ETA speed. The current connector scan has no bound<sup class="ref"><a href="#src-40" title="src/shell/body_planner.nim:399-435 (unbounded connector scan)">40</a></sup>, so the new attach needs its own bound. One-based versus zero-based room ids. Colossal has 13,730 pairs and 27,460 directed edges. Per-seat danger rasters are 2.75 MB on colossal. The zone field is built on first use and needs a server seam. There are nine fixtures. The overlay must be separate from the mutable safe cache.</p>
+    <p>Simplifications accepted: one legality oracle. No room-repair BFS. No <code>portalArrival</code> array. No bucket in target identity. No prefix truncation. Class resolution before the arrived test.</p>
+
+    <h3>Round 2: REVISE, seven corrections, all accepted</h3>
+    <ol>
+      <li>The Euclidean heuristic was not admissible in 1/16 px units. The exact octile heuristic replaced it. Portal fields became uint8 next-hops. The cost oracle stays float.</li>
+      <li>Portal <em>sides</em> are the graph nodes, and routes store edge IDs with direction, because collapsed portal nodes let a room change skip the crossing cost.</li>
+      <li>The query assembles and validates the route descriptor in shared scratch before an atomic copy. The segment memo is shared and query-local, not per seat.</li>
+      <li>The local search cap is a latency-derived constant, never room size.</li>
+      <li>No <code>gameStartTick</code> snapshot, because it is -1 until <code>startGame</code>. The server passes the elapsed zone tick into the step.</li>
+      <li>The 8 px coverage becomes an exhaustive offline proof in subtask 02.</li>
+      <li>Room dry flags come from a per-room <code>maxDamageArrival</code>, and hazard pricing advances the ETA cell by cell.</li>
+    </ol>
+
+    <h3>Round 3: GO, with three implementation-proof notes folded in</h3>
+    <ol>
+      <li>Memo accounting: the shared segment-cost memo is counted in the retained shared total (§4.3, item 4).</li>
+      <li>The octile heuristic is computed on cell-index deltas, with the rounding rule stated in the oracle (§4.3, item 3).</li>
+      <li>An adversarial earliest-arrival hazard case is part of qualification (§7, last risk).</li>
+    </ol>
+  </section>
